                <head>348. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On February 5, Julian Amery, Under Secretary for Colonial Affairs, flew to
                    Nicosia to represent the British Government in a new series of discussions with
                    Archbishop Makarios over the issue of British bases on
                    Cyprus. Amery and
                        Makarios failed to reach an agreement and on February
                    8, the Governor of Cyprus announced that the date for the island’s independence
                    was further (and indefinitely) postponed. Amery returned to London on February 11 after further
                    unsuccessful discussions. On February 23, Amery returned to Nicosia to resume discussions with Archbishop
                        Makarios over the future of British bases on
                    Cyprus.</p>
            </div>
